  "content": {
    "text": "CONCLUDED\nLast Updated:\n21 hours ago\n'Privacy' Overshadows 'Agents' as Apple Announces New AI Efforts\nIn marked contrast to recent AI presentations from Alphabet and Microsoft, Apple shied away from drawing too much attention to so-called agents.\nAs the company unveiled new Apple Intelligence features during Monday's WWDC keynote, the terms \"agent\" and \"agentic were mentioned only three times, twice in reference to coding tools.\nAgents are software that can use an AI model to accomplish a complex series of tasks from a simple conversational command. A rapid increase in agents has stirred new worries about cybersecurity and privacy.",
    "text_blocks": [
      "CONCLUDED",
